# Optional server-only token, required only when a human creates a pull request.
# Copy to .env.local or configure this variable in the web server environment.
# Strict issue publication always uses the authenticated user's verified fork.
# Allow upstream public reads and PR creation, fork Contents write, and fork
# creation when required. Fine-grained token ownership/repository restrictions
# may prevent cross-owner use. See docs/THIRD_PARTY_JS_TS_FLOW.md and GitHub's
# fork API permission documentation. Never use a NEXT_PUBLIC_ token variable.
PATCHVERDICT_GITHUB_TOKEN=
